Falsifies `address_space_layout::verification::window_refuses_every_malformed_or_overrunning_window`.

The defect: `window` no longer checks that the length is a whole number of pages, so an unaligned length inside the band is accepted.

Expected to fail: the harness's `refused_inputs_never_reach_here` loop is reached, an unwinding failure, for an unaligned length.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -241,10 +241,6 @@
         start_virtual_address.is_multiple_of(PAGE_BYTES),
         "a window must start on a page"
     );
-    assert!(
-        bytes.is_multiple_of(PAGE_BYTES),
-        "a window must be a whole number of pages"
-    );
     let Some(end_virtual_address) = start_virtual_address.checked_add(bytes) else {
         panic!("a window must not wrap past the top of the address space");
     };
